WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:47.152
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:47.422 --> 00:50.383
I'm never going back to that life, Mama Yaya.

3
00:50.467 --> 00:51.718
Are you happy?

4
00:51.801 --> 00:54.220
-This is my life now. -Chiara.

5
00:54.304 --> 00:56.806
This is the life I chose.

6
00:59.893 --> 01:01.519
What do you mean "congratulations"?

7
01:01.603 --> 01:03.146
Don't you remember?

8
01:15.408 --> 01:17.994
Let's see who you're hiding, Sean.

9
01:33.676 --> 01:38.681
anyone who tries to mess with our lives again.

10
01:59.327 --> 02:00.620
It's time.

11
02:25.019 --> 02:28.481
But what if Chiara still has unfinished business at La Concordat?

12
02:28.565 --> 02:30.942
Could that be why someone still wants to reach out to her?

13
02:41.661 --> 02:47.667
No, Chiara isn't like that. She's changed so much.

14
02:49.836 --> 02:51.546
I've seen how happy she is.

15
02:52.589 --> 02:55.550
How much she loves the life they've built here.

16
02:55.633 --> 02:57.218
She wouldn't let anyone destroy that.

17
02:58.845 --> 03:01.431
If she did have unfinished business,

18
03:01.514 --> 03:03.516
she wouldn't be acting like this.

19
03:04.100 --> 03:06.019
Chiara is efficient,

20
03:06.102 --> 03:06.936
fast,

21
03:07.020 --> 03:07.937
quiet.

22
03:14.777 --> 03:17.280
Should I ask Chiara herself?

23
03:19.657 --> 03:20.825
No.

24
03:25.580 --> 03:28.291
I'm only asking for one promise.

25
03:28.875 --> 03:31.419
I never stopped waiting

26
03:32.670 --> 03:35.298
and preparing for this day.

27
03:36.883 --> 03:40.094
The day our dreams would finally come true.

28
03:45.308 --> 03:47.769
I've found a different dream.

29
03:48.269 --> 03:50.730
I've built the life I want.

30
03:52.774 --> 03:54.984
I did my part, Chiara.

31
03:56.110 --> 03:58.696
It's time for you to do yours.

32
04:13.628 --> 04:17.382
The first time I saw you, Chiara, I was shocked.

33
04:18.967 --> 04:22.136
I got used to seeing violence in this mansion,

34
04:22.220 --> 04:24.430
but you were different.

35
04:27.183 --> 04:30.353
You never cried. You never complained.

36
04:30.853 --> 04:34.899
You just silently took every hit and every beating.

37
05:17.692 --> 05:18.526
Chiara.

38
05:19.610 --> 05:20.445
Chiara.

39
05:23.489 --> 05:24.699
My dear.

40
06:28.179 --> 06:29.263
So,

41
06:29.889 --> 06:31.682
I came here.

42
06:37.688 --> 06:39.232
Then you came along.

43
06:43.569 --> 06:46.864
I just wanted to take care of you.

44
06:59.043 --> 07:00.002
Yaya,

45
07:00.670 --> 07:02.088
Mama Yaya,

46
07:03.297 --> 07:04.966
while you're here.

47
07:15.143 --> 07:16.227
You know…

48
07:40.209 --> 07:41.669
I guess that's what it is.

49
07:42.295 --> 07:43.671
For now,

50
07:43.754 --> 07:46.299
La Morte Bianca is the queen.

51
07:49.260 --> 07:53.014
But one day,

52
07:53.097 --> 07:54.599
you could be the Queen.

53
08:08.946 --> 08:10.239
You too.

54
08:47.026 --> 08:49.695
I didn't even understand what any of that meant.

55
08:50.738 --> 08:52.448
And so much has changed.

56
08:55.493 --> 08:58.454
I found a life I wanted to choose.

57
08:59.288 --> 09:01.874
And this is what I want now, not that.

58
09:04.293 --> 09:05.670
What do you think?

59
09:06.963 --> 09:09.882
You think everything that happened in your life was just a coincidence?

60
09:10.841 --> 09:11.842
No, Chiara.

61
09:13.553 --> 09:15.846
There's a reason you're still alive.

62
09:16.597 --> 09:20.601
There's a reason La Morte Bianca fell.

63
09:21.352 --> 09:23.813
There's a reason you were left behind.

64
09:27.066 --> 09:28.859
What are you saying?

65
09:31.946 --> 09:34.282
I waited 20 years for you.

66
09:35.283 --> 09:39.870
For 20 years, I prepared for this very moment.

67
09:43.249 --> 09:44.292
No.

68
09:49.297 --> 09:50.339
How?

69
09:51.841 --> 09:53.301
How could you be so sure

70
09:53.384 --> 09:54.969
that this day would come?

71
09:55.052 --> 09:56.971
That I'd still keep our promise,

72
09:57.054 --> 09:58.347
our plans?

73
09:59.056 --> 10:01.017
I didn't make sure.

74
10:01.100 --> 10:02.226
I prepared.

75
10:03.019 --> 10:06.897
While you thought you were running away from the kingdom,

76
10:07.565 --> 10:11.110
I was slowly preparing this for your return.

77
10:57.698 --> 10:59.992
You know, sir, the timing is just suspicious.

78
11:00.493 --> 11:02.495
Just a few days after Mikoy proposed to Chiara,

79
11:02.578 --> 11:04.038
something like this suddenly came up.

80
11:05.998 --> 11:08.459
I still haven't detected any high-risk foreign nationals

81
11:08.542 --> 11:10.419
who entered the country this past week.

82
11:15.257 --> 11:17.593
I think this person is Filipino.

83
11:23.099 --> 11:25.059
There's something else you need to know.

84
11:33.067 --> 11:34.652
When a leader is taken down,

85
11:35.569 --> 11:37.405
someone always takes their place.

86
11:38.406 --> 11:41.867
Our counterpart agencies have noticed something.

87
11:41.951 --> 11:44.620
There have been more internal killings.

88
11:44.703 --> 11:47.123
More families are disappearing.

89
11:47.706 --> 11:50.334
And even their former allies

90
11:51.127 --> 11:52.128
are suddenly disappearing off the map.

91
12:14.400 --> 12:16.861
There really wasn't another woman, babe.

92
12:16.944 --> 12:17.778
There really wasn't.

93
12:18.404 --> 12:19.738
Okay, even if you…

94
12:20.364 --> 12:21.782
even if you cut it off,

95
12:21.866 --> 12:23.784
you can fry it, chop it up, make sisig out of it,

96
12:23.868 --> 12:24.743
there really wasn't anyone!

97
12:25.327 --> 12:27.580
There really wasn't. No one.

98
12:32.543 --> 12:34.295
No, I mean…

99
12:36.046 --> 12:39.133
That woman wasn't my ex.

100
12:39.216 --> 12:41.051
She wasn't someone from my past either.

101
12:41.135 --> 12:43.804
Okay, there really was nothing. She wasn't a one-night stand either.

102
12:43.888 --> 12:45.514
There was nothing going on at all.

103
12:49.310 --> 12:51.437
-Sisig? -Yes.

104
12:52.980 --> 12:54.231
And so?

105
12:59.570 --> 13:03.491
Something happened in my life that became the most complicated chapter

106
13:03.574 --> 13:05.284
of my life, okay?

107
13:06.202 --> 13:08.496
I was completely broken that day.

108
13:09.788 --> 13:11.832
Then she suddenly came along.

109
13:12.458 --> 13:13.918
It's just… She was like

110
13:15.127 --> 13:16.545
a fairy godmother.

111
13:22.968 --> 13:24.261
But without a wand.

112
13:27.389 --> 13:30.518
She came into my life at the worst possible time.

113
13:31.602 --> 13:32.770
She helped me.

114
13:34.104 --> 13:35.731
She helped me get back on my feet.

115
13:36.315 --> 13:37.399
That's all.

116
13:37.483 --> 13:39.860
There was nothing romantic about it.

117
13:44.281 --> 13:45.449
So,

118
13:46.408 --> 13:49.787
a woman came into your life

119
13:49.870 --> 13:53.082
when you were heartbroken?

120
13:54.542 --> 13:55.668
And then,

121
13:56.502 --> 13:57.878
she saved you?

122
13:58.462 --> 13:59.296
Yes.

123
14:00.214 --> 14:01.048
But

124
14:02.299 --> 14:04.385
the way you're saying it makes it sound really bad.

125
14:04.468 --> 14:05.719
It's not like that!

126
14:05.803 --> 14:07.221
Because it really is bad!

127
14:07.304 --> 14:10.057
But, okay, I met her abroad!

128
14:11.016 --> 14:12.768
I met her abroad!

129
14:15.563 --> 14:16.647
Alice.

130
14:18.023 --> 14:19.316
Alice.

131
14:22.903 --> 14:25.364
Alice, Alice.

132
14:25.447 --> 14:27.032
Alice.

133
14:27.116 --> 14:28.367
That day,

134
14:29.702 --> 14:30.828
I thought my life was over.

135
14:34.373 --> 14:38.168
But because of her, I found hope again.

136
14:51.974 --> 14:55.895
So don't think that just because La Morte Bianca is gone

137
14:55.978 --> 14:58.105
La Concordat is over.

138
14:58.731 --> 15:01.817
That's not how these organizations work.

139
15:02.401 --> 15:06.071
When one falls, someone takes their place.

140
15:06.155 --> 15:07.448
And more often than not,

141
15:08.240 --> 15:09.742
they're even more dangerous.

142
15:12.119 --> 15:14.872
If someone is making a move around Mikoy and Chiara,

143
15:14.955 --> 15:16.749
we can't rule out

144
15:16.832 --> 15:19.668
that they're connected to La Concordat.

145
15:30.971 --> 15:33.933
Continue the profile, okay?

146
15:34.016 --> 15:37.102
Find what we're missing.

147
15:37.728 --> 15:39.313
Stay on high alert for now.

148
15:39.396 --> 15:42.191
No assumptions. We need facts.

149
15:48.489 --> 15:50.032
And in the mafia,

150
15:50.783 --> 15:54.954
the fight for the throne never truly ends.

151
15:58.082 --> 15:59.291
So,

152
15:59.792 --> 16:01.210
where is she now?

153
16:03.253 --> 16:05.214
She went back to her hometown.

154
16:07.758 --> 16:09.009
But

155
16:09.635 --> 16:12.137
why did you have to make it so suspicious

156
16:12.221 --> 16:13.555
just by talking to her?

157
16:14.723 --> 16:17.559
And you even went as far as switching SIM cards.

158
16:19.687 --> 16:22.147
Babe. You're an agent, right?

159
16:24.316 --> 16:27.403
You know there are people who don't want to be traced.

160
16:28.278 --> 16:31.365
So when I found out she was here, and she talked to me,

161
16:32.074 --> 16:33.534
I immediately started thinking.

162
16:34.410 --> 16:37.037
What if someone was monitoring my phone?

163
16:37.121 --> 16:39.164
And I didn't want her to get dragged into it.

164
16:40.499 --> 16:43.460
So I immediately bought a prepaid SIM.

165
16:43.544 --> 16:46.755
Then after one call, I threw it straight in the trash.

166
16:46.839 --> 16:48.382
Just a safety precaution.

167
16:55.014 --> 16:57.057
I guess you're just being protective.

168
16:59.518 --> 17:02.730
I really am protective of the people I love.

169
17:03.355 --> 17:04.690
And you're one of them.

170
17:12.239 --> 17:13.782
Let me make it up to you.

171
17:35.054 --> 17:38.932
We confessed our feelings, then we got married.

172
17:39.433 --> 17:41.351
So, are we officially together?

173
17:42.102 --> 17:43.187
Confession,

174
17:43.270 --> 17:45.731
fake wedding while drunk.

175
17:45.814 --> 17:47.274
Does that count?

176
17:50.194 --> 17:54.490
We can't just suddenly become boyfriend and girlfriend, right?

177
17:55.824 --> 17:58.619
Or maybe we need to go on a honeymoon first?

178
17:59.203 --> 18:02.414
Oh, Sofie, you're getting ahead of yourself again!

179
18:38.784 --> 18:43.497
What's the proper message to send after a wedding?

180
18:45.332 --> 18:46.792
Is there etiquette for that?

181
18:49.044 --> 18:50.129
Okay.

182
18:54.466 --> 18:55.300
No.

183
19:07.646 --> 19:11.692
She might think I'm serious about marrying her.

184
19:13.110 --> 19:14.027
Wait.

185
19:15.737 --> 19:17.531
Am I serious?

186
19:19.199 --> 19:23.787
Maybe he's just embarrassed, or maybe he was really just drunk.

187
19:25.664 --> 19:27.499
No, whatever.

188
19:30.294 --> 19:32.171
Oh, no. Oh, no, it sent!

189
19:49.730 --> 19:51.815
Good thing I'm out of load.

190
20:20.969 --> 20:23.805
Some information came in at the agency.

191
20:23.889 --> 20:25.098
It's not verified yet,

192
20:25.599 --> 20:28.894
so I can't give you the details.

193
20:29.728 --> 20:31.897
But it's enough

194
20:31.980 --> 20:35.525
for me to tell you to keep an eye on your surroundings for now.

195
20:36.276 --> 20:37.986
Is this about Chiara and the others?

196
20:38.570 --> 20:42.950
For now, I can't say yes, but I can't say no either.

197
20:44.117 --> 20:46.453
I'm just keeping my promise.

198
20:47.037 --> 20:48.205
Thank you.

199
20:48.288 --> 20:51.083
And Mario, until we're sure,

200
20:52.709 --> 20:56.964
let's just let them think it's only about the wedding.

201
20:57.547 --> 20:59.299
Okay, you're right.

202
20:59.841 --> 21:01.760
I'll handle things here.

203
21:14.815 --> 21:16.775
Fire! There's a fire!

204
21:16.858 --> 21:18.110
-Fire! -Mario!

205
21:18.193 --> 21:19.987
-Mario! -Mario!

206
21:20.070 --> 21:22.322
-Mario! -Mario!

207
21:22.406 --> 21:24.491
-Mario, there's a fire! -Mario!

208
21:24.574 --> 21:26.451
-Mario! -Mario!

209
21:26.535 --> 21:27.369
-Come on, hurry. -Let's go.

210
21:28.453 --> 21:29.496
Mario!

211
21:31.957 --> 21:33.208
Straight ahead!

212
22:14.249 --> 22:15.709
How are you?

213
22:17.794 --> 22:19.880
Unfortunately, still alive.

214
22:21.465 --> 22:23.800
Sometimes, that's enough.

215
22:24.426 --> 22:26.887
When we lose someone,

216
22:28.096 --> 22:30.182
we only have two choices.

217
22:30.682 --> 22:33.518
We can choose to follow them,

218
22:34.102 --> 22:37.189
or we can live with a purpose.

219
22:38.732 --> 22:40.067
Even now,

220
22:42.319 --> 22:44.654
I feel like everything is my fault.

221
22:46.698 --> 22:48.408
I couldn't save her.

222
22:50.660 --> 22:53.205
If only I had been braver.

223
22:56.333 --> 22:58.752
I wish Alice were still with me.

224
22:59.419 --> 23:02.214
I know what it's like to lose someone.

225
23:02.964 --> 23:05.217
But you know what's even more painful?

226
23:07.302 --> 23:10.889
Living your life without doing anything.

227
23:14.518 --> 23:16.186
For the rest of your life,

228
23:17.896 --> 23:20.941
we slowly give up.

229
23:21.900 --> 23:23.193
But they,

230
23:23.693 --> 23:25.737
they just keep living.

231
23:26.488 --> 23:28.573
They just keep hurting people.

232
23:31.576 --> 23:32.911
What else can I do?

233
23:34.246 --> 23:35.455
A lot.

234
23:36.039 --> 23:38.458
Don't waste your pain.

235
23:39.751 --> 23:40.919
Use it.

236
23:41.837 --> 23:44.548
Make it your reason to fight.

237
23:47.050 --> 23:49.010
And if I want

238
23:49.719 --> 23:54.432
to find whoever did this to Alice and me?

239
23:55.433 --> 23:57.936
You don't have to do this alone.

240
23:58.562 --> 24:00.063
I'll be with you.

241
24:00.647 --> 24:02.649
Let's help each other.

242
24:03.984 --> 24:06.278
While you seek justice,

243
24:08.280 --> 24:10.240
I'll help you learn to live again.

244
24:18.456 --> 24:21.251
Let's fill the emptiness with new reasons

245
24:21.334 --> 24:23.253
to live and fight.

246
24:42.814 --> 24:45.650
-because of the severity of his injuries. -Injuries?

247
24:45.734 --> 24:46.693
How is he?

248
24:46.776 --> 24:49.112
We still don't know if there was a fight

249
24:49.196 --> 24:51.364
or if he violated any rules inside.

250
24:54.659 --> 24:55.744
Not far.

251
24:55.827 --> 24:57.871
This is starting to feel like a security agency!

252
24:58.455 --> 24:59.289
How are you related to him?

253
24:59.372 --> 25:01.166
-He's my brother. -All right. You're good, bro-in-law!

254
25:01.249 --> 25:02.959
Could there be a reason for it?

255
25:03.501 --> 25:04.794
They're not like this before.

256
25:11.676 --> 25:12.677
Here's the thing.

257
25:12.761 --> 25:16.139
Do you think if Victor escaped, he'd come back?

258
25:16.223 --> 25:18.183
I'm just worried. Something's not right.

259
25:18.266 --> 25:22.687
And we both know that Senator Quintin is up to something dirty.

260
25:25.273 --> 25:26.816
I was just thinking.

261
25:28.652 --> 25:30.987
What if we don't go through with the wedding?
